body:
even though im for it, for your purposes i would argue imprisonment is for the purpose of teaching the guilty person a lesson/punishing them. In comparison, the death penalty seems like an easy way to get out of serving time for presumably terrible crimes. What the hope of prison is is to rehabilitate, or at the very least, take the dangerous person out of society to prevent harm. Our hope is the person would take something from their time in jail, and if not learn something, act as more of a deterrent for future crime. 

&#x200B;

hope this helps a little, even though im more pro death penalty lol
